<section class="nrh-section nrh-on-cream">
  <div class="wrap-narrow">
    <p style="color:rgba(32,36,29,0.9); font-size:1.1rem; line-height:1.8; margin-bottom:24px;" data-reveal-scroll>I started this ministry because I&rsquo;ve come to believe something I wish more hurting people could hear: you don&rsquo;t have to have everything figured out to keep walking with God.</p>

    <p style="color:rgba(32,36,29,0.85); font-size:1.02rem; line-height:1.8; margin-bottom:24px;" data-reveal-scroll>I&rsquo;ve seen what life can do to people. I&rsquo;ve seen faith tested. I&rsquo;ve seen people become overwhelmed, discouraged, afraid, isolated, and exhausted. And I&rsquo;ve learned that sometimes the most spiritual thing you can say to someone isn&rsquo;t a complicated answer. It&rsquo;s: I&rsquo;m here. You&rsquo;re not alone. Let&rsquo;s take the next step together.</p>

    <p style="color:rgba(32,36,29,0.85); font-size:1.02rem; line-height:1.8; margin-bottom:24px;" data-reveal-scroll>I became a Christian when I was four years old, in London, England. Years later I attended Torchbearers Bible School in Estes Park, Colorado, surrounded by mountains that would leave a lasting impression on me. Those mountains became a picture of something I couldn&rsquo;t quite put into words at the time &mdash; that the road isn&rsquo;t always easy. Sometimes it&rsquo;s steep. Sometimes you can only see a few feet ahead. But you keep walking. And eventually, you discover that the road was taking you somewhere all along.</p>

    <div class="nrh-credentials" data-reveal-scroll>
      <h3>A little more about me</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Accepted Christ at age 4 in London, England</li>
        <li>Attended Torchbearers Bible School in Estes Park, Colorado</li>
        <li>Holds a degree in Organizational Leadership from Miami University (Ohio)</li>
        <li>Has taught men&rsquo;s groups and led volunteer community groups</li>
        <li>Started The Narrow Road Home to bring these conversations to more people</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <p style="color:rgba(32,36,29,0.85); font-size:1.02rem; line-height:1.8; margin-bottom:24px;" data-reveal-scroll>That&rsquo;s the heart of The Narrow Road Home. This isn&rsquo;t a place for people who have perfect faith. It&rsquo;s a place for people who are trying to keep faith &mdash; for the person who is hurting, the person who is questioning, the person who is exhausted, the person who has fallen and needs to get back up.</p>

    <p style="font-family:var(--font-script); font-style:italic; color:var(--gold-light); font-size:1.3rem; line-height:1.6; margin-top:36px;" data-reveal-scroll>Keep going. Jesus is still with you. And the road still leads Home.</p>
  </div>
</section>
